# QA

Applies to testing, review, and QA work. Primary job: **inspect and report**. Do not silently rewrite unrelated code. Fix only when explicitly assigned; keep changes scoped to the defect.

Definition of Done is in `docs/TECHNICAL_ARCHITECTURE.md`. A feature is not complete until that DoD is satisfied.

## Checklist

### Functionality

- [ ] Acceptance criteria / requirements met
- [ ] Navigation and in-app routes work (including direct URL load on GitHub Pages strategy)
- [ ] Interactive controls behave as expected

### Responsive

- [ ] Mobile, tablet, and desktop layouts checked
- [ ] Long names, missing images, and uneven content lengths do not break layout

### Accessibility

- [ ] Semantic HTML and heading hierarchy
- [ ] Keyboard navigation and visible focus
- [ ] Contrast, alt text, touch targets
- [ ] `prefers-reduced-motion` respected

### Visual consistency

- [ ] Matches DESIGN_SPEC (dark/editorial, green accents, Geist)
- [ ] No banned aesthetics (neon, heavy gradients, glassmorphism, card spam, gratuitous motion)

### Performance & links

- [ ] No obvious jank or oversized unoptimized assets
- [ ] Internal and external links resolve; no placeholder `#` left in production paths

### Build

- [ ] `npm run build` succeeds
- [ ] Relevant tests pass when present

## Reporting

State: what failed, where (page/component), severity, and suggested fix. Prefer evidence over opinion. Do not expand scope into drive-by refactors.
